(127105, 6013, 1041, '<td valign="top">mmmmm. future wine.  yummy.  it looks pretty dry out there.<br/><br/>challenge met -- yes<br/>composition / appeal -- so so.  composition is fine, i like the harvester on the left to add some color, and if i look closely, i can also spot the grapes, but, to be honest, this isn''t the most exciting shot to me personally.  i am also not sure what i would suggest to make it a little more appealing for me ... sorry.<br/>technical -- good<br/>overall -- 5<br/>gr8photos   :)</td>', 'mmmmm. future wine.  yummy.  it looks pretty dry out there.challenge met -- yescomposition / appeal -- so so.  composition is fine, i like the harvester on the left to add some color, and if i look closely, i can also spot the grapes, but, to be honest, this isn''t the most exciting shot to me personally.  i am also not sure what i would suggest to make it a little more appealing for me ... sorry.technical -- goodoverall -- 5gr8photos   :)', '2002-09-24 12:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(127106, 6013, 4143, '<td valign="top">Postcard quality</td>', 'Postcard quality', '2002-09-24 14:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(127107, 6013, 656, '<td valign="top">I''d have liked to see more of the progression of the vines into the distance, maybe shooting more down the gaps than into the vines.  Maybe even getting really close to a vine, so a bunch of grapes fills some of the foreground, while showing the rows leading off to the background ?</td>', 'I''d have liked to see more of the progression of the vines into the distance, maybe shooting more down the gaps than into the vines.  Maybe even getting really close to a vine, so a bunch of grapes fills some of the foreground, while showing the rows leading off to the background ?', '2002-09-24 23:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(127108, 6013, 3540, '<td valign="top">Nice landscape shot.  Looks like it was a great day to shoot.</td>', 'Nice landscape shot.  Looks like it was a great day to shoot.', '2002-09-25 06:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(127109, 6013, 772, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting photo... I can actually see a couple of the grape bunches on the vines... There are a few suggestions that I think may help this particular photo a bit... If you have the capability on your camera, a polarizing filter would remove quite a bit of the haze and blue cast that is showing in the distance of this image... also, I think that possibly showing some length on the rows between the vines would create a nice leading line into the horizon... good shot :) - setzler</td>', 'This is an interesting photo... I can actually see a couple of the grape bunches on the vines... There are a few suggestions that I think may help this particular photo a bit... If you have the capability on your camera, a polarizing filter would remove quite a bit of the haze and blue cast that is showing in the distance of this image... also, I think that possibly showing some length on the rows between the vines would create a nice leading line into the horizon... good shot :) - setzler', '2002-09-25 15:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(127110, 6014, 3102, '<td valign="top">Nice use of humor... well composed shot without being too busy.</td>', 'Nice use of humor... well composed shot without being too busy.', '2002-09-23 02:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(127111, 6014, 2764, '<td valign="top">I''m back like I promised.  I love this picture!  The only suggestion I would make is to leave a little wine in the bottle.  It''s friendlier and the red would balance the lower half of the shot which needs a hit of color.  The red shoes and the fiesta lights are top heavy colory wise.  It is a lovely shot that tells a great story.  The shoes, the "older" feet up on the table.  The place setting is perfect.  All the lines in te photo point of towards the missing lady.  She the table cloth lines, the napkins, the legs, all lead the eye and mind to where her face might be.  And the upright bottle interrupts that line, being the cause of why the center of interest is actually off the page.  Moving this up to a ten, the image has stuck with me all week  PS it has a universal appeal because we all know a version of that woman, my friends name is Pauline.</td>', 'I''m back like I promised.  I love this picture!  The only suggestion I would make is to leave a little wine in the bottle.  It''s friendlier and the red would balance the lower half of the shot which needs a hit of color.  The red shoes and the fiesta lights are top heavy colory wise.  It is a lovely shot that tells a great story.  The shoes, the "older" feet up on the table.  The place setting is perfect.  All the lines in te photo point of towards the missing lady.  She the table cloth lines, the napkins, the legs, all lead the eye and mind to where her face might be.  And the upright bottle interrupts that line, being the cause of why the center of interest is actually off the page.  Moving this up to a ten, the image has stuck with me all week  PS it has a universal appeal because we all know a version of that woman, my friends name is Pauline.', '2002-09-23 12:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
